I added this README to address several Things and discuss the future of SCH (Salah-Code-Lab).

Over the next few months, I will be busy focusing on personal matters and won't be able to dedicate as much time. The repositories will not be taken down; however, while they will still be maintained, updates will not be as active as before. I will continue to accept issues, feedback, and support (if the user contacted me via Session).

I won't have enough time to publish mitigations. I was previously expected to publish a mitigation for ShieldCrash, but those plans were canceled.

The main reason is that I couldn't get the exploit to work.
If anyone knows how to get it running, please let me know.
During my testing across Windows versions 21H2, 24H2, and 25H2, it consistently failed to execute.
I didn't just run a single instance and Pray; I ran multiple instances simultaneously and retested it over ten different times.
I also compiled the code myself rather than relying on the precompiled executable, but it still didn't work.
As a result, the vulnerability was unachievable in my environment. Even after testing it under specific conditions for days on end, it remained non functional.
Because of this, I cannot tell if my mitigation actually works, and I prefer not to stand/stay on assumptions a lesson I learned the hard way.

Regarding the YouTube channel: I know I previously mentioned working on a new video, and I was, but I struggled to figure out how to present the ideas effectively. After all, I am neither a content creator nor a video editor.

As for when I will return, I honestly do not know. do not wait for or expect a specific return date.

But as for now SCH Will stay online and accept Critics, issues, support, but will be less active and more Focused on the Projects owned by myself only

Until i come back, 

Farewell.
